  "tokens_v4": {
    "comment": "Cross-implementation V4 token vectors (spec 2.5.2 shapes). One 8-sat proof per token, mint https://mint.test, unit sat, keyset nut13_v3.keyset_id, C fixed. The `si` CBOR map carries k (bearer scalar), e (ephemeral E), i (internal key K), u (NUMS offset, present iff i is H + u*G), t (serialized leaves). The two encoders legitimately differ on things NUT-00 leaves free: cashu-ts writes the short (8-byte) keyset id and orders the top-level map m,u,t; nutshell writes the full 33-byte id and orders it t,m,u. What must agree is the spend_info: each side decodes BOTH strings to the same fields, and reproduces its own string exactly, so encoder drift shows up here.",
    "mint": "https://mint.test",
